   233	[[configurable-collection-implementations]]
   234	==== Configuring collection implementation types
   235	
   236	The built-in implementation for a supported interface can be replaced with an entry in `mapstruct.properties` at the root of the mapping compilation classpath:
   237	
   238	[source,properties]
   239	----
   240	mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.List=com.example.CustomList
   241	mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.Map=com.example.CustomMap
   242	----
   243	
   244	The processor option `-Amapstruct.configurationFile=config/mapstruct.properties` selects another resource by relative path on that same classpath. The resource is not loaded from the annotation processor path. The default resource is optional, while an explicitly selected resource must exist.
   245	
   246	Configured implementations must be publicly accessible concrete classes assignable to the named interface. They must preserve the interface's unbounded type parameters and provide a public no-argument constructor that declares no checked exceptions. If a public `int` constructor without checked exceptions is also available, MapStruct passes the source size as its initial capacity. Implementations generated in a later annotation-processing round are supported. An applicable object factory still takes precedence over the configured implementation.
